{%- comment -%}
  Paste this into the TRMNL Private Plugin "Markup" editor (Full tab) for
  the pictures plugin (Polling strategy). Field names match the JSON
  produced by fetch.mjs.

  Top: the Game Boy bird, shown at exactly 2/3 size so every Game Boy
  pixel is a clean 2x2 block. Under it, centred: a clock drawn with your
  own handwritten digits (digits/0.png-9.png, made by generate-digits.mjs,
  shown at full size = 3x3 blocks so it's easy to read). The time
  when the data was last updated is in the title bar, bottom right.

  The clock shows the time when TRMNL renders the screen (TRMNL's "now"
  is UTC, so we add your TRMNL account's time zone offset). E-ink doesn't
  tick, so it's the time of the latest refresh - it's at most one refresh
  interval behind.

  No "image-dither" anywhere (it would soften the pixel blocks), and
  image-rendering: pixelated keeps the blocks crisp if anything is scaled.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign utc_offset = trmnl.user.utc_offset | default: 3600 -%}
{%- assign hhmm = "now" | date: "%s" | plus: utc_offset | date: "%H%M" -%}

<div class="layout layout--col layout--center" style="gap: 10px;">
  {%- comment -%} zoom 2/3: each 3x3 Game Boy block -> exactly 2x2 px {%- endcomment -%}
  <img src="{{ image_url }}" style="zoom: 0.6667; image-rendering: pixelated;">

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center;">
    <img src="{{ digits_url }}/{{ hhmm | slice: 0 }}.png" style="image-rendering: pixelated;">
    <img src="{{ digits_url }}/{{ hhmm | slice: 1 }}.png" style="image-rendering: pixelated;">
    <img src="{{ digits_url }}/colon.png" style="image-rendering: pixelated;">
    <img src="{{ digits_url }}/{{ hhmm | slice: 2 }}.png" style="image-rendering: pixelated;">
    <img src="{{ digits_url }}/{{ hhmm | slice: 3 }}.png" style="image-rendering: pixelated;">
  </div>
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  <span class="title">{{ title | default: "Bilder" }}</span>
  <span class="instance">{{ index }} / {{ gallery_size }}</span>
  <span class="instance" style="margin-left: auto;">{{ updated_display }}</span>
</div>
